==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|heimskr||of a person- foolish, silly; who seldom leaves their home}}, from any related form of {{suffix|non|heimr|t1=home, abode|-skr}}. Equivalent to {{suffix|is|heim|skur}} by {{l|en|surface analysis}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|is|eimskʏr|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{is-adj|heimskari|heimskastur}}

# [[stupid]], [[foolish]], [[dumb]]
#: {{ux|is|Ógn er hann '''heimskur'''.|Oh how very '''stupid''' he is.}}
#: ''Að gera einhvern '''heimskan'''.'' (''synonym:'' {{m|is|forheimska}})
#:: To '''stultify''' someone.
#: {{syn|is|heimskulegur}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|heimskt er heimaalið barn}} (travel broadens the mind; homish is the home-bred bairn)

====Related terms====
* {{l|is|heimska}}
* {{l|is|Heimski}} (a nickname; compare the cognomen {{m|is|Brutus}}, from {{m|la|brūtus||heavy, unwieldy; dull, stupid}})

